--
Base-specifier pack expansion over a partial specialization's LEADING
NON-TYPE pack ([temp.variadic]/5.2): the __tuple_leaf<_Indx>... bases
are dropped (bases()=0, components()=0).  Root under
cpp11_libcxx_tuple / tuple_basic / apply_basic.  The type-pack
analogue is fixed (cpp11_tuple_leaf_no_body).  A first extension
attempt (non-type element recovery in the base expander) did not fire
-- the leading pack's values are not in pack_expr_map/spec_bindings at
base-expansion time; needs its own session.
Fixed 2026-08-04: the spec-pattern re-deduction admits empty trailing
packs ([temp.spec.partial.match]/2) and the base expander handles
every bound pack including non-type value packs ([temp.variadic]/5.2).
